xpense→Income, description, amount 125.50→200.75, category, and tax-related off. Row updated to 'QA Test Income - Updated | Sales Revenue | REF-QA-001 | +$200.75' with blank tax column. Delete also confirmed removing a row and updating totals.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created category 'QA Test Category' (Expense, Blue) which appeared with 0 transactions/$0; edited it to 'QA Test Category - Updated' with Rose color, change persisted; deleted it successfully and it disappeared from the list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changing transaction type from Expense to Income in the edit form reset category to 'Select category' and restricted the category dropdown to income categories only (Sales Revenue, Consulting, Interest Income, Other Income); selected category 'Sales Revenue' was retained on the saved transaction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggled Tax Related off during edit; saved transaction row shows blank Tax column instead of ✓. Earlier creation test showed toggling it on produced a ✓ in the Tax column.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combining search='Strategy' + type=Income + category=Consulting + date range Dec 1-31 2024 returned exactly 1 matching transaction (tx-6); clicking 'Clear Filters' restored all 19 transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing required fields not identified to user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Add Transaction form completely empty (no description, no amount, no category) did not create a transaction, but no error message, inline validation text, or aria-invalid indicator appeared anywhere in the dialog to tell the user what was missing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"