 (via edit form toggle) immediately removed it from the 2024 Tax Summary: transaction count dropped from 18 to 17 and Total Taxable Income decreased by $42.50 to $47,550.00, with tx-9 absent from the tax-related transactions list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding a $1,000 'Sales Revenue' income transaction, Categories page 'Sales Revenue' entry updated its transaction count from 3→4 and total from $36,750→$37,750, confirming category counts/totals update correctly on transaction change.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking 'Print Report' on the 2024 Tax Summary triggered the print action with no new console errors (error count remained at 1, same pre-existing React key warning unrelated to printing).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table shows columns Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, Tax, Actions; footer shows Total Income and Total Expenses for the current result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inaccurate monthly totals / stale balance\", \"actual\": \"Reports page for August 2026 (the current month, containing the newly added $1,000 income transaction) shows Income $0, Expenses $0, Profit +$0, and \\\"No income this period\\\" — it does not include the new transaction at all, so monthly report totals do not accurately reflect underlying transactions. Additionally, Dashboard Total Balance ($74,931) does not reflect the new +$1,000 transaction, making the balance stat inaccurate. (Monthly Income/Expenses/Profit stats and Recent Transactions list on the Dashboard were accurate.)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision for sub-$500 values\", \"actual\": \"Income vs Expenses bar chart on Dashboard has a